      "problem": "For the random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{E}[X]=4$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=5.$ Find $\\text{E}[XY].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are *independent* random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]\n$$\n\nIn this case, however, we don't know whether $X$ and $Y$ are independent. Therefore, $\\text{E}[XY]$ is impossible to determine using only the given information.",
